260
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,533
It got stuck when we crossed the bubble!

261
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:32,520
This bubble, it's a double structure.

262
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:36,980
A normal ship would crash
because there's nothing but air.

263
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,920
We're about to run into another bubble.

264
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,300
You guys ready?

265
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:46,130
Water?

266
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:01,060
This current is really strong.

267
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,680
Help me!

268
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:09,120
I can't breathe!

269
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:11,810
Crap!

270
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,474
Four of us can't swim!

271
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,580
Come on!

272
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:26,850
Freeze!

273
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,360
Nani! Bravo!

274
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,070
Dammit!

275
00:15:37,153 --> 00:15:38,420
I can't resist the current!

276
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:55,400
That's one way to get in.

277
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,172
Pretty reckless, though.

278
00:15:57,740 --> 00:16:01,097
Well, we could still go in after
them if you want to, Hammond.

279
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:04,004
No way to know if they're
alive or dead, though.

280
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,887
Yeah, let's track them down.

281
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,957
We can't let Neptune's army get their
hands on them first, now can we?

282
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:15,657
But before we do anything, we should go
back to Noah and tell the boss what's up.

283
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:20,240
I think he'd want to know that the
man who ruined Arlong's plan is here.

284
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,350
Hey!

285
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,717
Take a look.

286
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:36,697
I'll look.

287
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:37,697
I won't.

288
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,097
Maybe I'll look.

289
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:40,297
Who cares if I look?

290
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,697
Now he's moving.

291
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:42,977
He moved.

292
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:44,117
No, he didn't.

293
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,097
He might have moved.

294
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:48,220
Who cares if he moved?

295
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:53,797
Alright, he's alive.

296
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:54,780
Thank goodness.

297
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:01,900
Where am I?

298
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:03,620
Oh, Luffy-chin

299
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,320
It's been a while, hasn't it?

300
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,460
So how are you feeling?

301
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:17,097
Hey, it's Kuma.

302
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:18,857
It's nice to see you!

303
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:22,237
Oh, Kuma, you've got so lovely?

304
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:23,260
Kuma

305
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:29,720
Wait a minute, if Kami's here, we
made it to Fishman Island after all?

306
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:30,820
Yeah, we did!

307
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,037
From what I understand,

308
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:35,597
we were about to drown, but then we
were rescued by a bunch of mermaids!

309
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,510
That's right!

310
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:39,257
Sanji Chopper and I just
woke up a few minutes ago.

311
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:40,837
Guess we're pretty lucky, huh?

312
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,157
Lucky enough to wake up in Kami's house.

313
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,780
Here, catch. Uh-oh!

314
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,400
So this is your house?

315
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:47,910
My bad!

316
00:17:47,993 --> 00:17:50,357
I know I was supposed to
pick you guys up on Sabo Odi,

317
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,440
but I was thinking that
was another month from now.

318
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:54,620
That's okay.

319
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,118
Where is everybody?

320
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,220
Well, uh, it looks like we got separated.

321
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,720
Goodness, I hope they're safe.

322
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,200
So they're lost?

323
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,877
Well, I'm sure it'll turn out okay, right?

324
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:08,790
They're fine.

325
00:18:08,873 --> 00:18:10,917
The Bonehead can't do much underwater.

326
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,600
But the Robot and Mosshead are probably
with them, so I wouldn't worry. Right.

327
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:17,526
Everything will be just fine.

328
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:19,860
I hope I get to see them again soon.

329
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:21,740
Anyway, here you go.

330
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:26,431
I'm sure you're all freezing, so I made
some soup that'll warm you right up.

331
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:28,090
Daddy!

332
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:31,120
Cold seaweed soup! It's yummy!

333
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,180
It's cold?

334
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,970
That's not right!

335
00:18:40,053 --> 00:18:42,577
How are you supposed to get
bored if the soup is cold?

336
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:43,560
I'm sorry!

337
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,940
I'm such a failure!

338
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:49,000
The soup is great, Kuma.

339
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:52,340
I'm warmer already.

340
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,917
That doesn't make sense.

341
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,020
Come on, let me try some too!

342
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,177
Your clothes are dry, everybody.

343
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:02,117
They're dry.

344
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,657
No, they're not dry.

345
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:05,417
Your clothes might be dry.

346
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:06,971
Who cares if they're dry?

347
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:14,040
You keep care of our clothes too?

348
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,220
Well, thanks

349
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,360
Who are those little guys?

350
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,941
Oh, there's some friends of mine.

351
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:22,917
The Medica Mermaid Quintuplets.

352
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:27,800
I'm Ichka, I'm Nika, I'm Sanka,
I'm Young, and I'm Young too.

353
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,024
Wait, why are there two Yonkas?

354
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,517
They're really fast swimmers
and pretty clever as well.

355
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,430
Yeah?

356
00:19:34,513 --> 00:19:35,560
Nice to meet you.

357
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,197
I've got a lot of neat
friends here, actually.

358
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,397
This is the seafloor of the Mermaid Cove,

359
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:43,480
home to the girls' dorm of
the famous Mermaid Cafe.

360
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,450
Huh?

361
00:19:45,533 --> 00:19:46,363
The girls' dorm?

362
00:19:46,446 --> 00:19:49,197
Oh, it's just this cute little
cafe where I work as a waitress.

363
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:52,104
We have a lot of pretty
mermaids there on staff.

364
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,350
Sachi!

365
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,480
Don't die!

366
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,420
I won't die! No, no!

367
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:02,357
I swore I made a promise to myself that

368
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:05,397
for the entire time I
was on Fishman Island,

369
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:08,420
I wouldn't get a nosebleed and pass out.

370
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:15,740
And I've held out for this long,
so I deserve a reward, right?

371
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:17,730
Pathetic.

372
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,370
I know.

373
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:21,366
Why don't we go up there now?

374
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:23,893
I'll introduce you to all of my friends.

375
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,200
Whoa, a turtle!

376
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,680
Sea turtle elevator, huh?

377
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:34,500
Could you give us a lift, Mr.

378
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:35,450
Turtle?

379
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:42,460
This is a coral apartment complex.

380
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:45,257
The dorms are at the very
bottom, so rent's cheap.

381
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:49,222
The top floor is the most expensive
because it gets natural light.

382
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:50,690
Hmm.

383
00:20:50,773 --> 00:20:51,848
Does that mean you're poor?

384
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,980
And what about Hachi and Papagu?

385
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:57,207
Hatchan got beat up real
bad about a year ago.

386
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:58,997
Oh, yeah, I heard about that.

387
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:02,117
He was protecting the sunny
forest back on Sabaori, right?

388
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,917
Hatchan came from the Fishman District,

389
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,977
so that's where he's been
resting and recovering.

390
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,657
I haven't had the chance
to see him lately,

391
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:10,017
but from what I hear, he's
getting better all the time.

392
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:11,540
Huh? He's okay?

393
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:14,637
Yeah, but it's kind of
a rough part of town.

394
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:16,440
If you guys go along with me,

395
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:18,517
I wouldn't mind heading over
there to visit him, though.

396
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,430
Let's do it!

397
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:21,777
I've been wanting to
thank him face to face!

398
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:23,460
Sure, you got it.

399
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:29,260
And, well, as for Papa Goo, he's
a super famous fashion designer.

400
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:34,364
So he lives in a big, fancy mansion in the
high-class district of Fishfrily Hills.

401
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:38,017
I'm supposed to deliver
some clams over there today.

402
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:39,157
You want to come with me?

403
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:43,080
Wait, he's your pet, but you two
don't live in the same place?

404
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:47,517
Yeah, cause that area is a
little out of my price range.

405
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:49,820
We have better clams here anyway!

406
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,470
Huh?

407
00:21:51,553 --> 00:21:54,517
Hey, what's that drinking
straw looking tube, Dial?

408
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:55,620
Oh, that thing?

409
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:59,077
That's the water road, the
bubble craftsman built it.

410
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:02,717
And when mermaids or fish
get inside it, well, hold on!

411
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,500
Here, let me show you.

412
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:11,480
It's the surface!

413
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:14,100
We made it! Luigi!

414
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,230
Look!

415
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:18,060
I'm swimming in the sky!

416
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,800
Wait a sec!

417
00:22:23,060 --> 00:22:26,354
If we're underwater, why do
we see a sky full of clouds?

418
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:28,800
Hey, Kuma! Huh?

419
00:22:29,020 --> 00:22:29,940
It's a girl!

420
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:32,060
Where's that coming from?

421
00:22:32,540 --> 00:22:33,880
Hey, guys!

422
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:37,337
Are these your pirate friends?

423
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:40,185
I guess that means they
didn't drown after all.

424
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:44,897
You didn't come in through the
entrance like you're supposed to,

425
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:46,215
so we were concerned.

426
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:49,397
Well, hi there.

427
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:51,777
You're not as scary as I thought you'd be.

428
00:22:51,860 --> 00:22:52,920
So you broke in?

429
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:54,219
That's pretty hot.

430
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:56,459
I kind of have a thing for pirates.

431
00:22:57,980 --> 00:23:00,300
It's like a real-life fairy tale!

432
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:01,660
A coral paradise!

433
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,300
A whole cone full of mermaids!

434
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:09,400
What's the matter with Soji now?

435
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:13,072
He didn't even cry this hard
when he left the Breath egg.

436
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:16,530
Finally!

437
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:21,380
I found my all-blue after all these years!

438
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:26,000
Are you sure about that? Really?

439
00:23:27,540 --> 00:23:29,580
Here, let me introduce everybody.

440
00:23:29,980 --> 00:23:32,098
That's Luffy-chin, he's the captain.

441
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:34,140
Yeah, nice to meet you.

442
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,100
Sachi-Chin's the crybaby.

443
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:38,200
The nose guy is Usopp-Chin.

444
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:39,440
That's me.

445
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,780
And the raccoon is Chopper-Chin.

446
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:43,160
Not again!

447
00:23:44,940 --> 00:23:46,500
Why are you crying?

448
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,540
Come over here.

449
00:23:49,780 --> 00:23:51,780
Let's dance in the water together.

450
00:23:56,820 --> 00:23:58,900
Okay, I get it.

451
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:01,420
This is obviously too good to be true.

452
00:24:02,460 --> 00:24:04,660
Maybe I'm destined to die today.

453
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:06,000
That's dark!

454
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:09,797
What the heck happened to you in the
last two years to make you this gloomy?

455
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:12,821
Isn't this supposed to be
the land of your dreams?

456
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:16,680
You crack me up, Sanji.

457
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,529
I don't think he's joking!

458
00:24:19,260 --> 00:24:20,090
Hey,

459
00:24:20,173 --> 00:24:23,177
that barrel over there is the one that
drifted in with all Kamey's friends, right?

460
00:24:23,260 --> 00:24:24,090
What's in it?

461
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:25,640
Maybe treasure?

462
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:27,597
Uh, I don't know.

463
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:30,677
It's sealed pretty tightly,
so it's got to be important.

464
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:31,590
Yeah?

465
00:24:31,673 --> 00:24:33,660
I think we should open it.

466
00:24:38,380 --> 00:24:39,210
Interesting.

467
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:43,300
So Straw Hat finally made
it to our turf, did he?

468
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:44,740
Good for him.

469
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:46,670
Right.

470
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,494
What are we going to do about it, boss?

471
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:54,600
I want you to bring him here.

472
00:24:55,820 --> 00:24:56,860
And quickly.
